Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal
Description: type text on Wayland through the RemoteDesktop portal
 xdptype is a wtype replacement for Wayland compositors that do not
 implement the virtual-keyboard protocol, such as GNOME (mutter). It sends
 keysyms through the xdg-desktop-portal RemoteDesktop portal, so it needs
 no access to /dev/uinput. The permission dialog is shown once; the grant
 is remembered with a restore token.
 .
 Non-ASCII text (Polish, German, the euro sign, ...) is typed as-is,
 without guessing the keyboard layout.
